<title>POLAND: Polish minimum T-bill prices fall at tender.</title>
<headline>Polish minimum T-bill prices fall at tender.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of Polish T-bills fell at today's primary auction on total demand of 1.02 billion zlotys against a 1.2 billion zloty offer, the finance ministry said. The treasury sold a total of 638 million zlotys worth of T-bills.  </p>
<p>   T-bill	    8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week 52-week</p>
<p>   new min price   96.75    95.00    90.48     --	82.45</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    --     (95.08)  (90.55)    --     (82.60)</p>
<p>   new max price   97.02    95.30    90.80     --	83.18</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    --     (95.32)  (90.85)    --     (83.20)</p>
<p>   offer	     400.0    200.0    200.0     --	400.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded   158.5    242.1     55.5     --	559.8</p>
<p>   bids accepted   154.0    215.9     47.6     --	220.8</p>
<p>   next auction    400.0    200.0    200.0     --	500.0</p>
<p>NOTE. Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
